<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios-Jan 29.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios-Jan 29.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Highest and lowest price earnings ratios for Australian companies included in the 320-company All Ordinaries Index based on closing prices on Tuesday. P/E based on rolling 12 months earnings.</p>
<p>Highest 10</p>
<p>Rank Name		     P/E    Close</p>
<p> 1   Portman Min	   349.21   2.20</p>
<p> 2   Niugini Min	   214.39   2.98</p>
<p> 3   Countrywide-PP	187.10   1.16</p>
<p> 4   Mayne Nickless	172.19   7.80</p>
<p> 5   Colonial Coml	 122.95   2.25</p>
<p> 6   Adel Bton Cement    116.67   1.61</p>
<p> 7   Forrestania Gold     90.68   2.53</p>
<p> 8   Herald Rsc	     85.84   0.97</p>
<p> 9   Westral Forest	 78.26   2.16</p>
<p>10   Energy Equity	  76.26   1.06</p>
<p>Lowest 10</p>
<p> 1   Dominion Min	    1.95   0.85</p>
<p> 2   Consol Rutile	   3.70   0.90</p>
<p> 3   Premier Inv	     4.62   0.82</p>
<p> 4   BTR Plc		   6.13   5.70</p>
<p> 5   Parbury Ltd	     6.25   0.74</p>
<p> 6   OLS Asia Hldgs	  6.72   0.80</p>
<p> 7   Aust Gold Rsc	   7.12   1.30</p>
